  "description": "Attempts to derive absolute boiling and freezing temperatures strictly from the q-ideal gas law (q-PV = nRT) without fitted scaling factors. Computes the cohesion energy from the h²-suppressed H-bond network, then sets T_boil = S_q / (n_q R). With the naive choice n_q = [2]_q (the dimension of the Hopf base exploring S²), this over-predicts T_boil by a factor of 4.26x to 6.45x (H2O 6.45, HF 5.04, NH3 4.26) and T_melt by 1.38x to 2.56x. This demonstrates that the true entropy of vaporisation ΔS_vap requires a more sophisticated topological partition function (likely involving the full Reeb flow phase space) rather than just the bare dimension [2]_q. Result is recorded honestly as open.",
